{"name":"Deep Shadow","hex":"#514a3d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deep","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extending, reaching or positioned far from a point of reference, especially downwards.\nExtending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively.","Extending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Far, especially far down through something or into something, physically or figuratively.","In a profound, not superficial, manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep"},{"term":"shadow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark image projected onto a surface where light (or other radiation) is blocked by the shade of an object.","Relative darkness, especially as caused by the interruption of light; gloom; obscurity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unofficial, informal, unauthorized, but acting as though it were.","Having power or influence, but not widely known or recognized."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shadow","blocks":[{"text":"A shadow is a dark area on a surface where light from a light source is blocked by an object. In contrast, shade occupies the three-dimensional volume behind an object with light in front of it. The cross-section of a shadow is a two-dimensional silhouette, or a reverse projection of the object blocking the light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg/330px-The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Park_grid.JPG/500px-Park_grid.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wi